// home/niri/hosts/unclebeam-thinkpad.kdl — THIS machine's displays.
//
// One file per host, and Nix picks which one gets symlinked to
// ~/.config/niri/host.kdl (home/niri.nix, keyed on
// osConfig.networking.hostName). So config.kdl carries NO hostname branch,
// and the PC's outputs are never loaded on this machine.
//
// Everything below is a HARDWARE FACT — with one caveat this first round:
// resolutions/scales/positions are measured (carried over from the
// hyprland host file, which read them off this machine), but two of the
// output NAMES need first-login verification. niri matches the FULL
// "Make Model Serial" string — no prefix matching (unlike hyprland's
// desc:) — and a string that's even one character off silently never
// matches, leaving that panel on auto-config with no error. The Gigabyte's
// name below is VERBATIM from `niri msg outputs` in the first niri era
// (note "CO., LTD." with a comma — hyprland prints the same EDID as
// "CO. LTD." without it, so neither tool's output can be assumed for the
// other). The MSI has never run under niri and is derived from hyprland's
// desc, full placeholder serial included. On the FIRST niri login run
// `niri msg outputs` and correct the names verbatim if they differ; this
// file is an out-of-store symlink and niri live-reloads on save.
//
// Physical layout: the Gigabyte sits stacked directly ON TOP of the MSI,
// and the laptop is open to the LEFT of the MSI with their BOTTOM edges
// level (the laptop sits on the desk, the monitors are up on a stand).
//
//                      ┌────────────────────────┐
//                      │ GIGABYTE  0,-1440      │  y -1440 .. 0
//                      └────────────────────────┘
//    ┌──────────────┐  ┌────────────────────────┐
//    │ eDP-1        │  │ MSI (main)  0,0        │  y     0 .. 1440
//    │ -1920,240    │  │                        │
//    └──────────────┘  └────────────────────────┘
//     x -1920 .. 0      x     0 .. 2560
//
// `position` is in LOGICAL pixels, i.e. AFTER scale — same rule as
// hyprland, same classic mistake to avoid: both externals are 4K at scale
// 1.5 => 2560x1440 logical, so the top one is at y = -1440, not -2160. The
// laptop is 2880x1800 at 1.5 => 1920x1200 logical; bottom-aligning against
// the MSI's bottom edge (y = 1440) gives y = 1440 - 1200 = 240, and
// x = -1920 puts its right edge flush against the MSI's left edge.
//
// No workspace pins and no undocked hook (the hyprland file needed both):
// niri's workspaces are dynamic and PER-MONITOR — each output owns its own
// stack, undocking moves the orphaned workspaces to the live output
// automatically, and a solo boot just starts on eDP-1's first workspace.
// The whole "solo login lands on workspace 9" bug class is gone.

// Main: MSI PM271UPXW12G, 27" 4K, on USB-C. The 0x01010101 serial is a
// placeholder MSI ships on many panels (hyprland's file trimmed it off its
// prefix match; niri needs the full string, so it stays). 4K120 exceeds
// HBR3 and needs DSC over the Thunderbolt DP tunnel — this machine has a
// history of tunnel instability (repeated "DP tunnel activation failed"
// with the old Dells, 2026-08-01). Measured fallback if it blanks or
// re-enumerates: mode "3840x2160@60.000".
output "Micro-Star Int'l Co. Ltd. PM271UPXW12G 0x01010101" {
    // EXPLICIT 120, not omitted-for-highest like the PC's modes — this
    // panel tops out at 120 so they'd agree today, but spelling it out
    // documents the tunnel-bandwidth decision shared with the Gigabyte
    // below. If niri's modeline decimals differ it warns and auto-picks;
    // check `niri msg outputs` on first login.
    mode "3840x2160@120.000"
    scale 1.5
    position x=0 y=0
    // Where a docked login lands (niri focuses the first output only when
    // nothing says otherwise; solo boots land on eDP-1 since this output
    // is absent).
    focus-at-startup
}

// Above: GIGABYTE M28U, 28" 4K. Name is niri-verbatim (see header). 120
// chosen deliberately over the panel's 144 ceiling: it matches the MSI,
// and both externals share ONE Thunderbolt DP tunnel on a machine with a
// history of tunnel flapping — the spare bandwidth is worth more than
// 24 Hz nobody will notice. Measured fallback: "3840x2160@60.000".
output "GIGA-BYTE TECHNOLOGY CO., LTD. M28U 22060B005352" {
    mode "3840x2160@120.000"
    scale 1.5
    position x=0 y=-1440
}

// Left: the built-in Samsung OLED. Named by CONNECTOR — an internal panel
// never renumbers, reports no usable serial, and eDP-1 is the clearer
// name (same choice the first niri era made). Scale 1.5 divides both axes
// exactly (2880/1.5 = 1920, 1800/1.5 = 1200) — no fractional-remainder
// blur. Refresh omitted: niri picks the highest (120). No VRR: OLED
// flicker (the first niri era measured it on this panel).
output "eDP-1" {
    mode "2880x1800"
    scale 1.5
    position x=-1920 y=240
}
